            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for chalk, then the Kannada for a ruler."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಯುದ್ಧ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಯುದ್ಧ — yuddha — \"a war; a battle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಯುದ್ಧದ ಫಲಿತಾಂಶ ಹವಾಮಾನದ ಮೇಲೆ ಅವಲಂಬಿಸಿತ್ತು. yuddhada phalitāṃśa havāmānada mēle avalambisittu. The outcome of the war depended on the weather."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With ಮಾಡು it makes a verb: ಯುದ್ಧ (yuddha) ಮಾಡು, to fight a war."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಯುದ್ಧ (yuddha) is borrowed from Sanskrit yuddha, \"fought\", and as a noun \"a battle\", the past participle of the root yudh, \"to fight\" (CDIAL 10499). Kannada keeps the Sanskrit form whole, as it does many learned nouns."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
