          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸೈನಿಕ (sainika) is borrowed from Sanskrit sainika, \"belonging to an army\", and as a noun \"a soldier\" (Monier-Williams). It is built on senā, \"an army\", with the ending -ika, \"one who belongs to\"."
            }
          ]
